# Canonical identities for git log / shortlog / blame.
#
# All 15 commits here are authored as jim.galasyn@hotmail.com, but the author name
# appears both as "Jim" and as "Jim Galasyn". Both map to one canonical form.
#
# The second mapping is defensive rather than corrective: no commit in this repo
# uses jim.galasyn@confluent.io. It is listed because the global ~/.gitconfig on at
# least one machine still sets that address, and a repo-local user.email does not
# survive a fresh clone — so a re-cloned checkout would silently start authoring
# with it again.
#
# Counts above are a snapshot; recompute with
#   git log --format='%ae' | sort | uniq -c
#
# Format: Proper Name <proper@email> <commit@email>

Jim Galasyn <jim.galasyn@hotmail.com> <jim.galasyn@hotmail.com>
Jim Galasyn <jim.galasyn@hotmail.com> <jim.galasyn@confluent.io>
